  "body": "## Summary\n\nDesign record for **#5994** (pure-package import policy — package classes per tier, with compile-fail fixtures), under the Roc library-import design **#5956** and worlds program **#5955**.\n\nThe deliverable is the policy table plus the fixture specification. This PR is documentation only: it changes no compiler, catalog, `world_caps.rs`, runtime-grant, or Roc package-syntax behaviour.\n\n```text\ndoc/2026-11-08T17-12-39Z_design_id_package_import_policy/…md   # the record\ndoc/README.md                                                    # record map\nplanning/architecture/README.md                                  # design index\n```\n\nWhat the record decides:\n\n- **Classify by transitive platform requirements**, not by package name or a self-asserted `pure` label. A package with an empty requirement set is pure; `random.u64` is a host request, so a package that uses it is standard-dependent (a PRNG with explicit state can still be pure).\n- **Declared package requirement set** is distinct from the world's requested ceiling and from the analyzer's `discovered_used` set. The import gate, the server/world ceiling, and per-world grants stay separate checks — compile success is never user consent.\n- **Uses #5958's tier vocabulary** (`standard`, `sandbox.fs`, `host.fs.read`, `net.out`) from open PR **#7599** rather than inventing a parallel scheme; extension tiers remain opt-in and off by default. Tier rows are marked provisional pending #5958.\n- **Class × tier matrix** with allowed/declared/checked columns, including the nuance that `standard` means the existing standard surface, not automatic grants (e.g. `loc.*` stays excluded from default ceilings).\n- **Fixture specification**: the literal “one compile-fail fixture per class” cannot apply to the pure class, so the contract is one **positive** pure fixture plus a **compile-fail** fixture per effectful class/profile mismatch, each asserting the missing module/capability. The existing `roc-cap-demo` supplies the standard-dependent negative; extension rows are specifications until those providers exist.\n- **Distinct from PR #6237** (the merged capability-dependent demo), which proves the mechanism end-to-end rather than pinning class rejections.\n- Open questions routed to #5956 (requirement encoding/resolution) and #5958 (final tier model); the extension I/O must stay behind the existing host-request broker/replay boundary, not direct ambient I/O.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Read back against this checkout: `pkgs/id/crates/id-core/src/world_caps.rs` (catalog, `DefaultCeiling`, PlatformModule set, `loc.*` exclusions), `pkgs/id/examples/roc-cap-demo/` (positive + both negative tests), `pkgs/id/scripts/roc-test.sh` (fixture wiring).\n- Existing negative fixture asserted, not just \"compiles or not\": `pf.RocCap` missing-module check in `roc-cap-demo-test.sh` lines 50–64.\n- Relative links from the new record resolve; `doc/README.md` and `planning/architecture/README.md` index lines resolve to the record.\n\n## Merge danger\n\n**Door:** two-way — a dated design record; superseded by a later record or amended by appending a section.\n**Blast radius:** low — documentation only, no CI-affecting files.\n\nRefs #5994, #5956, #5955, #5958, #5957\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796750122&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7764&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7764&signature=4b67724aeeac9455c15c2245b081f3816be09a9830231091e4279856a2757544\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7764?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
